.SH DESCRIPTION
.B feg_prism
implements the Kuratowski Calculus from Fractal Entropic Geometrodynamics
(FEG).  Spacetime is modelled as a locally finite partially ordered set
(causal set), generated by Poisson sprinkling into a 4D causal diamond.
The engine detects topological defects (Causal Prisms, K\d2,N\u bipartite
structures with topological mass N), performs K\d5\u threat absorption
(colour confinement), classifies particle generations by topological
signature, measures spectral dimensions and causal flux via random walkers,
and evaluates ten observer measurements (M1\(emM10) including the full
Standard Model Lagrangian parameter card with zero free parameters.
.PP
The simulation operates on pure integer logic and discrete combinatorial
topology \(em floating-point arithmetic enters only at the final
macroscopic averaging step.
.PP
FEG Prism is the successor to causal_set_sim, extending the original
four-measurement engine with six additional observables: the electroweak
sector (M5), quantum decoherence and the Born rule (M6), neutrino census
(M7), PMNS mixing matrix (M8), Higgs mechanism via topological drag (M9),
and the assembled SM Lagrangian card (M10).  The ensemble framework has
been rebuilt with adaptive Welford convergence, per-realisation checkpointing,
and a type-safe CSR graph abstraction with compile-time direction tags.
