.SH THEORY
.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SS "Axiom 1 \(em Causal Sets (from Vol I)"
Spacetime is a discrete partial order \(em a directed acyclic graph (DAG)
where each node is a spacetime event and each edge encodes causal influence:
.IR A " \(-> " B
means \(lqA can causally influence B.\(rq  The DAG is generated by Poisson
sprinkling
.I N
points into a 4D causal diamond (|t|\~+\~r\~\(<=\~T/2) with fundamental
density \(*r\~\(~~\~1.  The volume of the 4D causal diamond is
V\~=\~\(*pT\u4\d/24, giving T\~=\~(24N/\(*p)\u1/4\d.
.SS "Axiom 2 \(em Quantum Dynamics (from Vol II)"
The geometry and quantum phases of the causal set are evaluated over a
non-commutative von Neumann algebra.  Macroscopic geometry is emergent,
dictated by the quantum Fisher Information Metric (Petz metric) defined
over the density states of causal histories.
.SS "The Sole Principle of Interaction"
The entirety of microscopic network dynamics is governed by a single
mandate: the preservation of unitarity (probability conservation) across
discrete, non-commutative causal links.  All emergent forces and
geometric structures are homeostatic mechanisms enacted by the causal
network to satisfy this principle under the topological constraints of
Kuratowski's Theorem.
.SS "Hasse Diagram"
The transitive reduction of the causal DAG.  If A\~\(->\~B\~\(->\~C, the
direct edge A\~\(->\~C is redundant and is removed.  The Hasse diagram
retains only nearest-neighbour causal links \(em the skeleton of
spacetime.  The resulting graph is \fBtriangle-free\fR by mathematical
necessity: any triple (u, w, v) with u\(->\~w, w\(->\~v, u\(->\~v would
make u\(->\~v redundant.  This constraint is central to all subsequent
topology.
.SS "Causal Prism (Matter = Bipartite Knots)"
A Causal Prism (K\d2,N\u bipartite, N\~\(>=\~3) is a directed subgraph
with two poles (origin, destination) and N \(>= 3 intermediates.  Each pole
points to all intermediates (u\~\(->\~w\di\u, v\~\(->\~w\di\u), forming a
bipartite structure.  These defects anchor probability flow and define
particle-like spectral signatures.  CRITICAL: K\d4\u complete subgraphs
(4 mutually connected events) CANNOT exist in the triangle-free Hasse
diagram produced by transitive reduction.  The Prism is the correct
fundamental particle for a directed, triangle-free DAG.
.PP
The Three Geometries of the Causal Prism:
.RS
.IP I. 4
.B "Geometry of Order"
(Phase 1 input): Transitive Reduction produces a triangle-free DAG.  The
\(lqempty\(rq structure is not empty \(em it is a 4D vacuum whose Lorentz
invariance is emergent from redundancy removal on a Poisson process.
.IP II.
.B "Geometry of Matter"
(Prism detection): The Causal Prism K\d2,N\u is the unique topological
particle permitted by the triangle-free constraint.  Mass is not a
property added to a field \(em it is the integer count N of intermediate
causal paths.  The mass hierarchy (electron/muon/tau) reduces to N in
{3, 4, 5}.
.IP III.
.B "Geometry of Logic"
(O(N) algorithm): The 2-hop detection algorithm runs in O(N) because the
physics is local.  Hasse links have bounded proper time (\(*t\~\(<=\~8);
therefore K\d2,N\u poles must be within bounded causal distance.  Any
valid prism partner v of node u is reachable in exactly 2 hops through a
shared intermediate w.  This is a computational proof that physical
locality is an information principle.
.RE
.SS "Threat Contraction (Strong Force / Colour Confinement)"
By Kuratowski's Theorem, a graph is non-planar iff it contains a K\d5\u
or K\d3,3\u subdivision.  When an external node is connected to BOTH poles
of a Prism AND \(>=\~2 intermediates, it threatens the topological
stability and is absorbed (vertex contraction) into the higher-degree pole.
This is a discrete analogue of colour confinement \(em the topology
enforces that quarks cannot exist in isolation.
.SS "Spectral Dimension (Gravity via Random Walkers)"
The spectral dimension is defined as
.PP
.RS
d\dS\u(t) = \-2\~d(ln\~P)/d(ln\~t)
.RE
.PP
measured via undirected random walkers on the Hasse graph.  On a smooth
4D manifold, d\dS\u\~\(->\~4.  On the Hasse graph the vacuum d\dS\u
diverges (boundary saturation), while Causal Prism defects stabilise d\dS\u
at a finite value \(em matter modifies the effective geometry.
.SS "Causal Flux (Electromagnetism via Directed Walkers)"
Directed walkers following the arrow of time (cause\~\(->\~effect only).
The transmission probability from Gen1 particles to AntiGen1 measures
attraction (opposite charges); transmission from Gen1 to Gen1 measures
repulsion (same charges).  Normalised per-charge flux isolates the
intrinsic coupling strength (Vol\~II per-charge definition).
.SS "Three Generations (Kuratowski Limit)"
The Standard Model has three copies of matter.  In FEG the answer is a
strict topological obstruction: UV gravity defines a 2D topology, and
Kuratowski's Theorem forbids K\d5\u.  Causal Prisms are classified by
the \fBVol I phase function\fR \(*f(w) = sign(bulk_momentum[w]).  For each
prism P with intermediates {w\d1\u, \(el, w\dN\u}: g(P) = |{\(*f(w\di\u)}|
counts distinct phase values (generation number 1, 2, or 3), and
\(*F(P) = \(*S\(*f(w\di\u) gives the net phase (matter if \(*F \(>= 0,
antimatter if \(*F < 0).  Gen1 = g=1 \(AN \(*F\(>=0, Gen2 = g=2, Gen3 = g=3,
Anti1 = g=1 \(AN \(*F<0.  The constraint g \(<= 3 (at most 3 distinct sign
values: \-1, 0, +1) enforces exactly 3 stable generations.
.PP
Sterile prisms (\(*F = 0) are gravitationally active but
electromagnetically silent \(em dark matter candidates predicted by the
Phase-Coherence Theorem.
.SS "Ten Observer Measurements (M1\(emM10)"
FEG Prism implements ten measurement algorithms that extract the complete
Standard Model parameter card from the causal set topology:
.RS
.IP "M1" 4
Cover-time mass (topological inertia of prism-confined walkers).
.IP "M2"
Half-life census (cross-ensemble stability statistics).
.IP "M3"
Modulo path integral (NTT-based interference fringes).
.IP "M4"
Vacuum polarization (K\d3,3\u screening).
.IP "M5"
Electroweak sector (SU(2) chirality + U(1) port counting).
.IP "M6"
Quantum decoherence and Born rule verification.
.IP "M7"
Neutrino census (open prisms \(em frustrated K\d2,N\u).
.IP "M8"
PMNS mixing matrix (layered BFS wavefront propagation).
.IP "M9"
Higgs mechanism (topological drag via gauge propagation delay).
.IP "M10"
SM Lagrangian card assembly (zero free parameters, post-hoc).
.RE
