.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SH MODULES
.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SS "phase1 \(em Phase 1: Vacuum Generation"
Poisson sprinkling in a 4D causal diamond + Hasse diagram construction.
Two tiers: sparse A\(S2 transitive reduction (N\~\(<=\~15k) and direct
geometric construction via the Occupied Cell Index (N\~>\~15k).
.TP
.BI "sprinkle(" n ", rng) \(-> (Vec<[f64;4]>, f64)"
Rejection-samples
.I n
points inside |t|\~+\~r\~\(<=\~T/2 with T\~=\~(24N/\(*p)\u1/4\d giving
density \(*r\~\(~~\~1.  The volume of the 4D causal diamond is
V\~=\~\(*pT\u4\d/24.
.TP
.BI "build_hasse_sparse(" pts ") \(-> (coords, CsrGraph<Directed>, momentum)"
Full causal closure \(-> sparse A\(S2 reduction.  Edge (i,j) is a Hasse
link iff A\(S2[i,j]\~=\~0.  Used for N\~\(<=\~15,000.  Returns time-sorted
points, a directed CsrGraph, and the per-node bulk momentum vector.
.TP
.BI "build_hasse_direct(" pts ") \(-> (coords, CsrGraph<Directed>, momentum)"
Direct geometric construction using the OCI (Occupied Cell Index) \(em a
spatial indexing paradigm that replaces naive geometric shell enumeration
(96% empty cells) with per-time-layer lists of occupied cells, queried
via binary search.  Three termination valves: Valve 1 (degree cap at
MAX_HASSE_DEGREE), Valve 2 (Alexandrov volume short-circuit: all causal
candidates transitively blocked \(-> break), Valve 3 (adaptive dry-shell
termination).  Returns cell-sorted points, a directed CsrGraph, and
bulk momentum.
.PP
Key concepts:
.RS
.TP
.B GridPoint
A spacetime event quantised onto an integer lattice for cache-coherent
traversal.  Points are sorted by cell index so that spatially nearby
events are contiguous in memory.
.TP
.B OCI (Occupied Cell Index)
Paradigm shift from geometric to spatial indexing.  Builds per-time-layer
lists of occupied cells, sorted by X coordinate, queried via binary
search.  Reduces inner-loop cost from O(shell_volume) to
O(occupied_cells).
.TP
.B Termination Valves
Three valves control the dt-shell search.
.B "Valve 1 (Degree Cap):"
A node with \(>=\~MAX_HASSE_DEGREE (15) descendants has fully populated
its causal shadow; further links are redundant.
.B "Valve 2 (Alexandrov Short-Circuit):"
If every causal candidate in a dt-shell is transitively blocked (the
Alexandrov set between u and v is non-empty), further shells have
strictly larger Alexandrov volume and will also be blocked.  Breaks
immediately when degree \(>=\~1.
.B "Valve 3 (Dry-Shell Termination):"
Two consecutive dry dt-shells (no new Hasse links) with \(>=\~2 existing
descendants triggers cutoff.
.RE
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "phase2 \(em Phase 2: Kuratowski Contraction"
Pure integer topology \(em zero floating-point.  Core identification \(->
Causal Prism (K\d2,N\u bipartite) detection \(-> threat contraction \(->
generation classification.
.PP
Algorithm:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Core selection: top 10% of nodes by Hasse degree.
.IP 2.
Causal Prism formation: forward-forward 2-hop search.  For each core
node u with out-degree \(>=\~3 (minimum valence pruning), traverse
u\~\(->\~w\~\(->\~v to collect pole candidates.  Candidates v with
in-degree\~<\~3 are skipped before the belly intersection.  Belly =
children(u)\~\(*e\~parents(v); if |belly|\~\(>=\~3, the pair forms a
K\d2,N\u Prism.  Greedy best-partner selection maximizes N per pole.
.IP 3.
Threat contraction: any external node connected to BOTH poles AND \(>=\~2
intermediates is merged into the higher-degree pole.
.IP 4.
Generation classification (Vol I phase): Prisms classified by
\(*f(w) = sign(bulk_momentum[w]).  g(P) = |{\(*f(w\di\u)}| gives the
generation number (1, 2, or 3); \(*F(P) = \(*S\(*f(w\di\u) gives the
net phase (matter if \(*F \(>= 0, antimatter if \(*F < 0).
.IP 5.
Phase-coherence mass decomposition: visible mass = \(*S|\(*F(P)|,
dark mass = \(*S(N \- |\(*F(P)|), gravitational mass = \(*SN.
.IP 6.
Self-energy coupling constants: Q\dtopo\u = \(*S|\(*F|\u2\d / \(*SN\u2\d,
\(*a = Q\dtopo\u / (8\(*p), \(*W\denergy\u = 1/Q\dtopo\u \- 1.
.IP 7.
Intermediate phase census: count nodes with \(*f = +1, 0, \-1 across all
committed prism bellies.
.IP 8.
Build defect CSR: add pole-completion edges for committed prisms,
constructing the Kuratowski-contracted CsrGraph<Undirected>.
.RE
.TP
.BI "apply_defect(" n ", vacuum_csr, momentum) \(-> (DefectOutput, TopologySummary, Vec<CausalPrism>)"
Finds Causal Prisms (K\d2,N\u bipartite structures with belly nodes),
classifies them by topological signature into generations, performs threat
contraction, and builds the defect CSR by adding pole-completion edges.
The committed Vec<CausalPrism> is returned so that callers (e.g.\&
\-\-export\-slice) can access the raw prism geometry.
.PP
.B DefectOutput
struct fields:
.RS
.TP
.B vacuum_csr
Vacuum Hasse CsrGraph<Directed> (forward-only, cell-sorted).
.TP
.B defect_csr
Defect CsrGraph<Undirected> after threat contraction + pole-completion edges.
.TP
.B vacuum_core
