.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "phase3 \(em Phase 3: Spectral Dimension"
Random walk return probability measurement.  Two tiers: eigendecomposition
(exact, N\~\(<=\~3k by default; adjustable via
.BR \-\-eigen\-cutoff )
and Monte Carlo walkers (above the cutoff).
.TP
.BI "spectral_dimension(" steps ", p_vals) \(-> Vec<f64>"
d\dS\u(t) = \-2\~d(ln\~P)/d(ln\~t) via centred finite differences.
Forward/backward differences at the endpoints.
.TP
.BI "run_walkers(" head ", data, starts, steps, seed, merge) \(-> Vec<f64>"
Run W independent lazy-walk walkers in parallel (50% stay, 50% move to
random neighbour).  Parallel via Rayon.  Strict Finitism: all internal
accumulation uses u64 integer arithmetic; the single f64 division
count\~/\~W occurs only at the final return.  Optional merge map
resolves threat-contracted nodes to their canonical identity.
.TP
.BI "distribute_walkers(" starts ", n_walkers) \(-> Vec<usize>"
Distribute W walkers uniformly across a set of starting nodes.
.TP
.BI "run_transmission_walkers(" ... ") \(-> (Vec<f64>, Vec<f64>)"
Directed walkers (mandatory move along causal arrow).  Measures
transmission flux between particle generations (attraction and repulsion).
Same u64 integer accumulation as run_walkers.  Returns paired attraction
and repulsion probability vectors.
.TP
.BI "compute_eigen(" n ", rows, cols, steps, core) \(-> (WalkResult, WalkResult)"
Exact P(t) = N\u\-1\d \(*S \(*l\dk\ut from eigendecomposition of
S\~=\~D\u\-1/2\dAD\u\-1/2\d.  Returns (global, core) pair.
Complexity: O(N\(S3).
.TP
.BI "compute_monte_carlo_csr(" n ", head, data, steps, core, n_w, rng) \(-> (WalkResult, WalkResult)"
Zero-copy Monte Carlo variant \(em avoids rebuilding adjacency when CSR is
already available from Phase 2.  This is the hot path for large N
in-memory runs.  Returns (global, core) pair.  Complexity: O(W\(mut),
independent of N.
.TP
.BI "build_flux_csr(" vac_csr ", pts, merge_map, n) \(-> CsrGraph<Directed>"
Build directed flux CSR from vacuum CSR by filtering to forward-only
causal edges (t\du\u < t\dv\u) with merge-map resolution.  Used for
causal flux transmission walkers.
.PP
.B WalkResult
struct fields:
.RS
.TP
.B p
Vec<f64> \(em return probability P(t) at each measurement step.
.TP
.B ds
Vec<f64> \(em spectral dimension d\dS\u(t) derived from P(t).
.TP
.B ds_std
Vec<f64> \(em ensemble standard deviation of d\dS\u across M realisations.
Empty (vec![]) when M\~=\~1.
.RE
.PP
.B SpectralOutput
struct fields:
.RS
.TP
.BR vacuum ", " vac_core
WalkResult for global and core vacuum walkers.
.TP
.BR defect ", " def_core
WalkResult for global and core defect walkers.
.TP
.BR generations
[WalkResult; 4] for Gen1, Gen2, Gen3, AntiGen1.
.TP
.B sterile
WalkResult for sterile prism walkers (\(*F = 0).
.TP
.BR flux_attr ", " flux_repu
WalkResult for directed attraction and repulsion flux.
.TP
.BR flux_attr_norm ", " flux_repu_norm
Vec<f64> per-charge normalised flux: flux / |targets|.
.TP
.B mass
[f64; 4] per-generation mean topological mass.
.RE
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "graph \(em Type-Safe CSR"
Compressed Sparse Row graph with compile-time direction tag via PhantomData.
.B CsrGraph<Directed>
stores forward-only edges (past\~\(->\~future).
.B CsrGraph<Undirected>
stores both directions (symmetric).  The type tag prevents accidentally
passing a directed Hasse diagram to spectral walkers at compile time.
.TP
.BI "CsrGraph::new(" head ", data, n_nodes) \(-> CsrGraph<D>"
Construct from pre-built CSR arrays.  Panics if head.len() != n_nodes + 1.
.TP
.BI "CsrGraph::neighbors(" u ") \(-> &[u32]"
Sorted neighbor slice for node u.  Binary search is valid.
.TP
.BI "CsrGraph::degree(" u ") \(-> usize"
Degree of node u (O(1) from head difference).
.TP
.BI "CsrGraph::has_edge(" u ", v) \(-> bool"
Binary-search edge test (neighbors are sorted ascending).
.TP
.BI "CsrGraph<Directed>::symmetrize() \(-> CsrGraph<Undirected>"
Build the symmetric (undirected) version by adding reverse edges.
Each directed edge u\(->\~v produces both u\(->\~v and v\(->\~u entries.
Neighbor lists are sorted ascending.
.TP
.BI "CsrGraph<Directed>::reverse() \(-> CsrGraph<Directed>"
Build a reversed directed graph (swap all edge directions).  Used for
building parent adjacency from the forward-only Hasse DAG.
.TP
.BI "CsrGraph<Undirected>::unique_edges() \(-> Vec<(u32, u32)>"
Extract unique edges (u < v) for eigendecomposition.
.TP
.BI "build_directed_csr(" n ", rows, cols) \(-> CsrGraph<Directed>"
Build a directed CSR from unsorted (row, col) edge pairs with sorted
neighbor lists.
.TP
.BI "build_undirected_csr(" n ", rows, cols) \(-> CsrGraph<Undirected>"
Build an undirected CSR from unsorted (row, col) edge pairs where u < v.
Automatically adds reverse edges.
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "ensemble \(em Adaptive Ensemble"
.TP
.BI "run_ensemble(" n ", steps, walkers, ...) \(-> EnsembleResult"
Run the full adaptive ensemble.  Processes realisations in batches via
Rayon.  Between batches: Welford convergence check on mass_gen1, atomic
checkpoint write, and intermediate CSV snapshots.  Stops early when
relative SE \(<= target_error.
.TP
.BI "run_realization(" n ", seed, steps, walkers, eigen_cutoff, measure)"
Run Phases 1\(en3 for a single Monte Carlo universe: sprinkle \(->
Hasse \(-> Kuratowski \(-> spectral dimensions + generation walkers +
causal flux + optional M1\(emM9 measurements.
.TP
.BI "average_ensemble(" results ", steps) \(-> SpectralOutput"
Average P(t) across realisations element-wise, then recompute d\dS\u from
the mean P.  When M > 1, also computes per-step standard deviation of
d\dS\u and flux for error bars.  Physics: d\dS\u is non-linear in P(t),
so averaging P first ensures the ensemble-averaged spectral dimension
reflects the mean geometry.
.TP
.BI "aggregate_topology(" topos ") \(-> TopologySummary"
Merge TopologySummary structs across realisations: sum prism counts and
histogram frequencies, take max of max_intermediates, average masses,
recompute phase-coherence ratios from summed totals.
.PP
Checkpointing:
.RS
.TP
.BI "checkpoint::save(" dir ", params, spectral, topo, mean, m2)"
Atomic write of checkpoint to
.IR .checkpoint.bin .
Uses temp file + rename for crash safety.  Includes provenance hash for
cross-fork rejection.
.TP
.BI "checkpoint::load(" dir ", params) \(-> Checkpoint"
Load and validate a checkpoint.  Rejects if provenance hash, version,
or run parameters mismatch.
.TP
.B RunParams
Parameter fingerprint (N, seed, epsilon, tmax, eigen_cutoff, exec_mode).
Stored alongside checkpoint data so that
.B \-\-resume
can detect changed CLI arguments.
.RE
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "measure \(em Observer Measurements (M1\(emM10)"
Ten read-only measurement algorithms that extract physics from existing
simulation data.  All measurements are optional and activated via CLI
flags (\fB\-\-measure\-all\fR enables M1\(emM9;
\fB\-\-measure\-lagrangian\fR enables M1\(emM9 + M10).
.TP
.B "M1 \(em Cover-Time Mass (Topological Inertia)"
Measures the dynamical mass of each Causal Prism via coupon-collector
cover time on the defect CSR.  A confined random walker must visit
\fBevery\fR belly node before exiting at the destination pole.  Cover
time scales as O(N\~log\~N) \(em heavier generations (larger bellies)
require more causal ticks for full internal phase coherence.  If the
walker reaches the destination before full coverage, it reflects back
to the origin (incomplete phase update).  The K\d2,N\u hitting-time
theorem proves that simple origin\(->\~destination traversal is O(1)
regardless of N; cover time is the correct dynamical mass observable.
.TP
.B "M2 \(em Half-Life Census"
Cross-ensemble stability statistics.  For each prism, records
generation, belly size, and net phase.  Computes occupancy fractions
p(gen\dk\u\~|\~N) per belly size and stability ratios
\(*t(gen2)/\(*t(gen1), \(*t(gen3)/\(*t(gen1).  At N=5000, M=8:
occupancy fractions 4%/79%/17% match the zero-parameter occupancy
model prediction (2%/85%/13%).
.TP
.B "M3 \(em Modulo Path Integral"
NTT-based interference fringes from walker phases.  Walkers carry a
modular phase g\uS\d\~mod\~p (default: g=3, p=65537) where S counts
cumulative moves.  Per-node phase accumulation via AtomicU64.
Post-processing computes intensity (squared centred phase), classifies
constructive/destructive nodes.  Requires N\~\(>=\~50k for spatial
resolution.
.TP
.B "M4 \(em Vacuum Polarization"
K\d3,3\u screening at Gen1 prism free ports.  For each Gen1 prism,
counts candidate nodes that could extend it to K\d3,3\u (connecting to
both poles AND \(>=\~3 intermediates).  Screening factor =
n\daccepted\u\~/\~n\dattempted\u.  At N=5000: zero screening (vacuum
too sparse for K\d3,3\u), which is the correct finite-size behaviour.
Computes bare and screened alpha from port counting.
.TP
.B "M5 \(em Electroweak Sector (SU(2) Chirality + U(1) Port Counting)"
Per-intermediate chirality \(*x = (out_d \- in_d) / (out_d + in_d)
classifies handedness.  SU(2) doublets = min(n_left, n_right).
Free port counting on poles vs intermediates (MAX_HASSE_DEGREE = 15)
yields a topological charge Q\dtopo\u.  Weak filtering: only pole ports
are weak-active.  Causal filtering: only origin-pole ports contribute
(time-ordering).  The local Q\dtopo\u converges to 4/21 (Vol\~II,
Thm 6.3).  Per-generation chirality fractions measure parity violation.
.TP
.B "M6 \(em Quantum Decoherence (Born Rule Verification)"
Environment = nodes within 2 hops of both poles but not part of the prism.
Modular walkers (g\uS\d\~mod\~p on symmetric vacuum CSR) accumulate
phase per-node via AtomicU64.  Coherence = variance ratio of interior vs
environment modular intensities.  Directed path counting through prism
intermediates to environment nodes yields Born-rule |\(*y|\u2\d
predictions.  Binned comparison of predicted vs observed arrival
probabilities gives \(*x\u2\d goodness-of-fit.  Coherence decay
correlation vs 1/\(sr(env_size) measures decoherence rate.
.TP
.B "M7 \(em Neutrino Census (Open Prisms)"
Detect open prisms \(em high-degree core nodes whose forward belly fails
to converge onto a single destination pole (frustrated K\d2,N\u).
Open prisms are the causal-set analogue of neutrinos: no destination pole
\(-> no cover-time trapping \(-> near-zero mass; no backflow \(-> pure
left-handed chirality; unanchored belly size \(-> generation fluctuation
(flavour oscillation).  Per-candidate measurements: belly chirality,
escape time (walk to exit belly), and confined cover time (walk restricted
to belly subgraph).  Effective generation assigned by belly size thresholds.
.TP
.B "M8 \(em PMNS Mixing Matrix (Layered BFS Wavefront)"
For each open prism (neutrino) detected by M7, a BFS wavefront is
propagated through the directed vacuum CSR.  At each causal depth d,
the wavefront width determines the instantaneous generation (flavour).
Layer-by-layer generation transitions give the discrete topological
analogue of |U\dPMNS\u|\u2\d.  Convergence filter: children with
\(>=\~3 parents in the current layer are excluded (prevents premature
collapse into closed prism territory).  Output: 3\(mu3 row-stochastic
transition matrix, per-depth generation fractions, and survival statistics.
.TP
.B "M9 \(em Higgs Mechanism (Topological Drag)"
The photon (U(1)) propagates freely on the symmetric vacuum CSR via BFS.
The W boson (SU(2)) propagates only through left-handed nodes
(\(*x < 0, i.e.\& 2\(muout_deg < sym_deg).  BFS shortest path d\dbase\u
(photon) vs d\dchiral\u (W boson) between temporally distant prism pairs
(early/late quartiles).  Drag coefficient \(*m = (d\dchiral\u \-
d\dbase\u) / d\dbase\u is the emergent mass of the vector boson \(em the
topological cost of chiral confinement.  CDF diagnostic: BFS ball volume
for photon vs weak-filtered propagation gives an area-law verification.
.TP
.B "M10 \(em SM Lagrangian Card (Zero Free Parameters)"
Pure post-processing: assembles the full Standard Model parameter card
from M1\(emM9 results plus TopologySummary.  No graph traversal.
Missing measurements fall back to 0.0 so the card is always produced.
Key derived parameters:
.RS
.TP
.B Gauge sector
SU(3)\(muSU(2)\(muU(1), bosons 8/3/1, 3 generations.
.TP
.B Coupling constants
\(*a\dem\u = Q\dtopo\u/(8\(*p), sin\u2\d\(*q\dW\u = 4/17,
cos\u2\d\(*q\dW\u = 13/17, e = \(sr(4\(*p\(*a), g\d1\u, g\d2\u,
m\dW\u/m\dZ\u = \(sr(cos\u2\d\(*q\dW\u).
.TP
.B Gravity
G\dN\u = 1/(16\(*p) from Jacobson alpha-sweep plateau: G = 1/16.
.TP
.B Fermion masses
Cover-time mass topo per generation, mass ratios, CPT violation.
.TP
.B Neutrino sector
Count, escape-time mass proxy, chirality, PMNS matrix.
.TP
.B Higgs sector
Mean drag \(*m, CDF area ratio.
.TP
.B Dark sector
\(*W\ddark/vis\u, \(*W\denergy\u.
.TP
.B Quantum mechanics
Born \(*x\u2\d, coherence decay r.
.RE
