.TP
.BI "sha256(" msg ") \(-> [u8; 32]"
Minimal two-block SHA-256 implementation (msg.len() \(<= 119 bytes).
No external crate dependency.
.TP
.BI "utc_timestamp() \(-> String"
Generate an ISO-8601 UTC timestamp from the system clock.  Pure Rust
implementation without chrono dependency.
.TP
.BI "git_hash() \(-> &'static str"
Compile-time embedded git hash via env!("GIT_HASH") from build.rs.
.TP
.BI "git_dirty() \(-> bool"
Compile-time dirty-tree flag via env!("GIT_DIRTY") from build.rs.
.TP
.BI "commit_string() \(-> String"
Format the git hash with optional " (dirty)" suffix.
.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I N
Number of spacetime events (default: 5000).
.TP
.I M
Maximum ensemble realisations (default: 50).  This is the safety cap;
the ensemble may converge and stop earlier based on
.BR \-\-target\-error .
.TP
.I output_dir
Directory for results (default: current directory or
.I causal_set.toml
setting).  Created automatically if it does not exist.
.TP
.B \-\-stream
Force streaming mode (low RAM, writes edges to disk).
Currently not implemented in FEG Prism; will print an error.
.TP
.B \-\-inmemory
Force in-memory mode (fast, needs sufficient RAM).
.TP
.BI "\-\-seed " u64
Base seed for deterministic runs.  Each realisation uses seed + i.
Default: system clock nanos (real entropy).  The chosen seed is printed
at startup so non-seeded runs can be reproduced.
.TP
.BI "\-\-threads " usize
Maximum parallel realisations.  Default: auto (2 for N > 10M in-memory,
4 otherwise).  Capped at min(batch_size, max_ensemble).
.TP
.BI "\-\-epsilon " f64
Topological error tolerance \(*e for the Causal Resolution Theorem.
Default: 0.01.  Controls the number of spectral walkers:
W = (t\dmax\u / \(*e)\u2\d.
.TP
.BI "\-\-tmax " usize
Maximum diffusion time.  Default: 15.  The step sampling extends
to step 100 (dense 1\(en30, then even steps 32\(en100).
.TP
.BI "\-\-eigen\-cutoff " N
Eigendecomposition threshold.  Graphs with N \(<= cutoff use exact
eigendecomp; larger graphs use Monte Carlo walkers.  Default: 3000.
.TP
.BI "\-\-target\-error " f64
Relative standard error threshold for adaptive convergence.
Default: 0.01.  The ensemble loop stops early when the relative
standard error of mass_gen1 drops below this value.
.TP
.BI "\-\-max\-ensemble " usize
Maximum number of realisations (hard safety cap).  Default: 50.
.TP
.BI "\-\-min\-ensemble " usize
Minimum realisations before convergence checks begin.  Default: 8.
.TP
.BI "\-\-batch\-size " usize
Maximum realisations per parallel batch.  Default: 4.
Actual batch concurrency is min(batch_size, threads).
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Resume from a previously saved checkpoint.  Reads
.I .checkpoint.bin
from the output directory.  Rejects if provenance hash, version, or
run parameters (N, seed, epsilon, tmax, eigen_cutoff, mode) have changed.
.TP
.BI "\-\-export\-slice " PATH
Export a single realization's topology to a binary
.I .slice
file (bincode format) and exit.  Runs Phases 1\(en2 only (no spectral
walkers, no ensemble averaging).  The output contains 4D coordinates,
directed Hasse edges (past\~\(->\~future), and Causal Prism definitions.
Intended for feeding pre-computed topology data to external renderers
such as CausalAnim.
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-mass
Enable cover-time mass ratios (M1).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-halflife
Enable half-life census (M2).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-modulo
Enable modulo path integral (M3).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-vacuum
Enable vacuum polarization (M4).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-electroweak
Enable electroweak sector (M5).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-decoherence
Enable quantum decoherence and Born rule verification (M6).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-neutrino
Enable neutrino census (M7).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-pmns
Enable PMNS mixing matrix (M8).  Implicitly enables M7 (neutrino).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-higgs
Enable Higgs mechanism via topological drag (M9).
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-lagrangian
Enable SM Lagrangian card assembly (M10).  Implicitly enables M1\(emM9.
.TP
.B \-\-measure\-all
Enable all measurements M1\(emM9.  Does \fBnot\fR enable M10 (use
\fB\-\-measure\-lagrangian\fR for the full card).
.TP
.BI "\-\-modulo\-prime " u64
Prime modulus for M3/M6 (Fermat number).  Default: 65537 (F\d4\u).
.TP
.BI "\-\-modulo\-root " u64
Primitive root for M3/M6.  Default: 3.
.TP
.BI "\-\-modulo\-steps " N
Number of walker steps for NTT modulo accumulation (M3/M6).
Default: 500.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
