.TE
.SS "Causal Flux"
Directed walker transmission probabilities measure electromagnetic-like
interactions:
.TP
.B Attraction
Gen1 \(-> AntiGen1 (opposite charge, positive flux).
.TP
.B Repulsion
Gen1 \(-> Gen1 (same charge, lower transmission).
.PP
Normalised per-charge flux (Vol\~II definition) isolates the intrinsic
coupling strength independent of target population size.
.SS "Born Rule"
The M6 Born rule verification computes a chi-squared goodness-of-fit
between the predicted arrival probability (|number of directed paths|\u2\d
normalised) and the observed walker arrival frequency at environment
nodes.  Low chi-squared values validate that the discrete causal-set
walk statistics reproduce the continuous quantum-mechanical Born rule.
.SS "PMNS Mixing"
The M8 PMNS measurement produces a 3\(mu3 row-stochastic transition
matrix |U\dPMNS\u|\u2\d from layered BFS wavefront propagation through
open prisms (neutrinos).  Off-diagonal elements encode flavour
oscillation probabilities; diagonal elements encode survival probabilities.
Mean survival depth measures the average causal propagation distance
before the wavefront loses neutrino identity (width drops below threshold).
.SS "Higgs Drag"
The M9 Higgs measurement computes the drag coefficient
\(*m = (d\dchiral\u \- d\dbase\u) / d\dbase\u from BFS shortest paths
between temporally distant prism pairs.  Non-zero drag arises because the
W boson is confined to left-handed nodes (chiral subgraph), which is
sparser than the full vacuum graph.  The CDF ball-volume diagnostic
confirms that the weak-filtered frontier grows slower than the photon
frontier at all BFS depths.
